 {
  "event": 401,
  "id": "toolu_vrtx_01Nf6kYmuQciNUiZncwEajXJ",
  "tool": "slack_send_message",
  "context": "main",
  "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "ok": true,
  "result_event": 402,
  "channel": "D04UP2L3E3S",
  "thread_ts": "1770961200.890407",
  "text": "Here's what I'd do. Every issue in the LLC project has my call on it, and the sheet matches the project: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hqkCJcuj2s-qgzf7YrxXCmRD82paHYRAjiKCFFpIp6I/edit (in my Drive, shared with you and Blake)\n\n**What the LLC takes if Sunset can't sell it**\n• **Combo Fighter**: comes over either way, through Sunset's sale. I own it.\n• **Domino Delights**: comes over. It made $183.11 in January (warehouse daily revenue) and its prod account bills $140 now, so it covers its own hosting. You're handling it with Sunset. Its player support already goes to the email address.\n• **Zombie Match**: stays with HG. It made $0 in January and its AWS account still bills every month. CF doesn't need that account anymore.\n• **Services moving to the LLC by March 1**: DD prod AWS and CF's AWS (Blake moves them), and AppsFlyer free tier for CF (you set it up).\n• **Everything else stays with HG**: whatever we already cancelled or kept in #winddown, plus the build boxes, the dev/analytics AWS accounts, Figma (lapses Sep 11) and the dev accounts. The listings go with the games. Calm Play isn't used, since the LLC is the new one. The playable vendor is a one-off, so it's not in the plan.\n\n**Monthly cost, March through May: $450**\n• Billed to the LLC: DD prod AWS $140 + CF AWS $62 = $202\n• Already on Blake's card: Metabase $100 + dbt $100 + GitHub $48 = $248\n\n**Each of us carries $150 a month**\n• Me: $150 cash\n• You: $150 cash\n• Blake: covered by the $248 on his card. That's $98 over his third, so the LLC pays him back $98 a month out of our $300.\n\nTalk Monday."
 }
